{{- end }}
{{- end }}
{{- if $workstation }}
- User folders live under `~/files`: `downloads`, `docs` and `media` (pictures,
  music and videos). There is no `~/Desktop`, `~/Documents` or `~/Downloads`;
  `xdg-user-dir DOWNLOAD` gives the download folder.
{{- end }}
{{- if .gaming }}
- Gaming: GameMode.
{{- end }}

## Packages and dotfiles
{{ if $fedora }}
- dnf installs packages, with COPR for Starship, LazyGit, Klassy and Bibata
  cursors and Microsoft's repository for VS Code. Pinned GitHub releases add yazi and ya, gping
  (`~/.local/bin`) and fzf-tab (`~/.local/share/zsh/plugins`).
{{- else }}
- apt installs packages from the official Debian 13 repositories only. Pinned
  GitHub releases add what Debian lacks: chezmoi, nvim{{ if $workstation }}, uv, uvx, yq{{ end }} and
  actionlint.
{{- end }}
- To add a tool for good, add it to
  `~/.local/share/chezmoi/home/.chezmoidata/packages.yaml` and run
  `chezmoi apply`; the package script installs only what is missing and uses
  sudo.
- chezmoi manages the dotfiles. Edit the sources in
  `~/.local/share/chezmoi/home` (`.tmpl` files are templates), check with
  `chezmoi diff`, deploy with `chezmoi apply`. `scripts/verify.sh` in that
  checkout checks the machine.
{{- if eq .profile "server" }}
- A daily user timer (`dotfiles-update.timer`) pulls and applies file
  changes without the scripts; `just vps-update` in the checkout runs those,
  with sudo.
{{- end }}
- Settings for this machine only go in the local files, which chezmoi leaves
  alone: `~/.zshrc.settings`, `~/.zshrc.local`, `~/.zshenv.local`,
  `~/.gitconfig.local`, `~/.ssh/config.local`, `~/.tmux.conf.local` and
  `~/.config/kitty/kitty.d/*.conf`.

## Aliases and helpers in the user's terminal

This section is the reference for every alias and helper the managed
`~/.zshrc` defines; `tests/machine.sh` fails when one is missing here. Many
exist only when their tool is installed. `command NAME` or `\NAME` runs the
original command.

| Typed | Runs |
|---|---|
| `ls`, `ll`, `la` | eza with icons and directories first; `ll` and `la` add a header, Git status and ISO dates |
| `tree`, `lt`, `ltt` | `eza --tree`, at any depth, two or three levels |
| `cat` | `bat --paging=never --style=plain`: highlighted, and unchanged when piped |
| `cd` | zoxide's `z` |
| `..`, `...`, `....`, `-` | parent directories; the previous directory |
| `mkd`, `mkcd DIR` | `mkdir -p`; create a directory and enter it |
| `vi`, `vim` | `nvim` |
| `top` | `htop` |
| `fd` | `fd --hidden --exclude .git` |
| `grep`, `diff`, `ip` | the same command with colour |
| `df`, `du`, `free` | human-readable sizes |
| `open` | `xdg-open` |
| `helpme` | `tldr` |
| `lg`, `ai`, `air` | LazyGit; Claude; Claude resuming a session |
| `uvr`, `uvs`, `uva`, `uvp`, `pyi`, `pyls` | `uv run`, `sync`, `add`, `pip`, `pip install`, `pip list` |
| `sc`, `scu`, `jcf`, `jcu`, `jcb` | `systemctl`, `systemctl --user`, `journalctl -fu`, `-u`, `-b` |
| `reload`, `zshconfig`, `nvimconfig`, `dotfiles` | `exec zsh`; edit `~/.zshrc`; edit `~/.config/nvim`; `chezmoi cd` |
{{- if $fedora }}
| `y` | yazi; quitting with `q` moves the shell to yazi's last directory |
| `s`, `icat`, `kd` | Inside Kitty only: `kitten ssh`, `kitten icat`, `kitten diff` |
| `Ctrl+G` | navi cheat sheets (`~/.local/share/navi/cheats/dotfiles`) |
| `Tab` | fzf-tab: completion in fzf with previews; `<` and `>` switch groups |
{{- end }}
{{- if $fedora }}
| `dnfup`, `dnfi`, `dnfs`, `dnfrm`, `dnfinfo` | dnf upgrade, install, search, remove, info |
{{- else }}
| `aptup`, `apti`, `apts`, `aptrm`, `aptshow` | apt upgrade, install, search, remove, show |
{{- end }}

`DOTFILES_ENABLE_COMMAND_OVERRIDES=1` in `~/.zshrc.settings` also maps `less`
to bat, `grep` to rg, `find` to fd and `mkdir` to `mkdir -p`.

| Helper | Does |
|---|---|
| `fe`, `fcd` | pick a file with fzf and edit it; pick a directory and enter it |
| `frg PATTERN` | search contents with ripgrep, pick a match, open `$EDITOR` at that line |
| `fga` | pick changed or untracked files, with a diff preview, and stage them |
| `fh [QUERY]` | pick a history line and put it on the prompt for editing |
| `fkill [SIGNAL]` | pick processes and signal them, TERM by default |
| `psg QUERY` | search the running processes |
| `groot`, `gclone URL [DIR]` | enter the repository root; clone and enter |
| `gwip`, `gunwip` | commit everything as a timestamped WIP; undo only such a commit |
| `tm [NAME]` | create or attach a tmux session, named after the directory by default |
| `extract ARCHIVE` | unpack with the matching tool (rar and 7z need theirs installed) |
| `serve [PORT] [ADDRESS]` | `python3 -m http.server`, on localhost:8000 by default |
| `activate` | source `.venv` or `venv` |

The file pickers pass names NUL-delimited, so spaces and colons are safe.
`fe` and `frg` expect `$EDITOR` to name a program, not a command with flags.
